love is the feeling youre looking for and its living right here behind our door.  that line.  but the only love i can count on is mine for myself.  and yes writing and critiquing the tech industry is me finally exhaling.  instead of complaining and pointing out the stupidity i get the chance to take them on in an intelligent way as well as build in it as a sovereign.  i finally found where i fit in, getting the industry certifications and then critiquing the companies in their own language that i now understand. and your point about the dead still doing work because of what they left behind, that hit hard because a mirror of my becoming is my gift to my people and i want to give it them and them only free and clear and if i die without doing this it would be tragic.  that is why i put in 12-16 hour days i am driven to complete my work and find a distribution channel that leads directly to my people.  leo ai: **Foundational Black Americans (FBA)** is a lineage-based term for Black Americans who descend from enslaved Africans and free Black people who were in the U.S. during the country's founding and development \'97 as opposed to more recent Black immigrants to America https://worldhistoryedu.com/who-are-foundational-black-americans-the-history-behind-the-fba-identity/.\
\
**Key points:**\
\
- **The term itself** was popularized around 2019 by media personality and filmmaker Tariq Nasheed, though it describes a population whose history goes back centuries https://worldhistoryedu.com/who-are-foundational-black-americans-the-history-behind-the-fba-identity/.\
- **"Foundational"** emphasizes that these ancestors built much of the nation's economy, infrastructure, culture, politics, and national identity while enduring slavery, Jim Crow, and segregation https://worldhistoryedu.com/foundational-black-american-vs-african-american-what-is-the-difference/.\
- **It's not an organization.** The official FBA site explicitly states it is "not a group, organization, or movement with a designated leader" \'97 just a lineage designation for descendants of the Freedmen and early free Black Americans https://officialfba.com/.\
- **FBA vs. African American:** "African American" is a broad racial/national identity, while FBA claims a specific ancestral distinction \'97 descendants of people who experienced American slavery and its aftermath https://worldhistoryedu.com/foundational-black-american-vs-african-american-what-is-the-difference/.\
\
**Cultural elements:** The movement has its own symbols, like the Maroon Flag honoring escaped enslaved people who formed independent maroon communities in Southern swamps, and a holiday called *Arutisuse* ("Arise"), which commemorates escape attempts historically timed around the Christmas season https://officialfba.com/.\
\
Worth noting: some of the movement's historical claims (like tracing FBA origins to a 1526 slave revolt in what's now South Carolina/Georgia) are promoted by Nasheed's site but are contested, and critics have characterized parts of the narrative as revisionist history https://www.urbandictionary.com/define.php?term=Foundational+Black+American. \
