\fs38 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec2 I. The Pill and the Supply Chain\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f6\i\fs24 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Limitless
\f2\i0  (2011), directed by Neil Burger from Leslie Dixon's screenplay, adapted from Alan Glynn's 2001 novel 
\f6\i The Dark Fields
\f2\i0 , tells the story of Eddie Morra, a blocked writer who takes a designer drug \'97 NZT-48 \'97 and becomes the best version of himself overnight. The film was a hit. Its vocabulary escaped containment entirely: a decade later, "the real Limitless pill" is a functioning product category, and the supplement industry sells the fantasy by name.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 The film is usually read as a fantasy about unlimited intelligence. It is more honest than that. 
\f6\i Limitless
\f2\i0  is a movie about \strokec2 supply chains.\cb1 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 Watch what the plot actually worries about. The scenes with teeth are never Eddie's triumphs \'97 they are his procurement problems. He hoards: pills in the freezer, pills in a bag, pills taped behind fixtures. He negotiates with Vernon, the broker who dies holding the stash. He inherits Gennady's connection and a Russian mob debt. The third act is not about what Eddie can 
\f6\i do
\f2\i0  \'97 it is about whether he can 
\f6\i get more
\f2\i0 . Reviewers noticed: the two "plot holes" audiences most often cite are "never borrow from Russian mobsters" and "always secure your source of drugs" \'97 which is to say, the audience understood the movie's real stakes even while mislabeling them as sloppiness. The film's climax, in its own logic of persistence, is Eddie 
\f6\i acquiring the supplier
\f2\i0  \'97 buying the lab that manufactures the thing his existence now requires. When the story wants to show Eddie being smart about the future, it shows him becoming a supplier kingpin. That is the film's entire model of what it takes to keep being enhanced: \strokec2 vertical integration of a dependency.\cb1 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 And the source novel agrees about the price. In Glynn's 
\f6\i The Dark Fields
\f2\i0 , Eddie does not triumph; he dies alone in a motel room when the supply collapses \'97 the Faustian bargain closing on schedule. The film cut that ending. Dixon's screenplay \'97 which she held contract rights over \'97 replaced death with a Senate seat and an ambiguous final scene implying Eddie may no longer need the pill at all. The consequence was not overlooked. It was \strokec2 edited out\strokec3 , because consequence does not sell enhancement. The movie's most criticized element \'97 that cheat of an ending \'97 is the ideology showing: a fantasy this appealing cannot afford to show what happens when the supply runs out, so it simply declines to.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 Here is what the film never shows, because within its frame it 
\f6\i cannot
\f2\i0 : Eddie building something that keeps working \strokec2 after he stops taking the pill.\strokec3  Not more pills. Not a bigger stash. Not control of the lab. Something 
\f6\i decoupled
\f2\i0  \'97 an enhancement that lives outside his body, outside the supply chain, outside the frame in which the drug is the thing itself. The film is structurally incapable of imagining maintenance, delegation, or handoff, because its fantasy is pure, unmediated, personally-held capability. In the NZT frame, decoupling is impossible. The enhancement is the substance, and the substance must be swallowed.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 This paper is about the frame the movie is missing. The enhancement does not have to live in a body. It can live in files. And the supply question \'97 the question the entire third act runs on \'97 does not have to exist at all.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
