\fs38 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec2 II. NZT With an Invoice\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 The fantasy got its drug; reality got a subscription. The cognitive enhancement the film imagined arrived \'97 and it arrived exactly as the novel described it: a consumable, metered, and owned by a supplier. The dose form changed from pill to API, and the dependency got an invoice.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 The supply-chain evidence is not an argument. It is a published schedule. OpenAI's deprecations page lists model retirements on a rolling cadence \'97 snapshots notified in June 2026 shut down in December; a batch of GPT-4-era models killed October 23, 2026, eleven days after this paper's drafting. Even fine-tuned derivatives die with their base. This is the vendor's own document: \strokec2 the intelligence was never purchased. It was rented, and the lease ends on a date the vendor sets.\cb1 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 The rental terms are thinner than they look. Anthropic commits to "at least 60 days' notice" before retiring a model. OpenAI allows roughly six months. And the same model can have different lifespans on different shelves \'97 Claude Sonnet 4 left Anthropic's own API in June 2026 but survived on Amazon Bedrock until October 14, one day before this paper's finalization. \strokec2 The substrate's lifespan is not a property of the model. It is a property of the reseller.\strokec3  Eddie's problem exactly: the enhancement depends on which supplier still stocks it, and the supplier answers to no one.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 The deepest dependency is the quietest one. What users actually rely on is not the model's 
\f6\i function
\f2\i0  \'97 it is the model's 
\f6\i behavior
\f2\i0 : its tone, its latency profile, its formatting habits, its response length. When a model is deprecated and a replacement arrives, the functional output may survive while the behavioral envelope shifts under it \'97 and the prompts tuned to the old model's quirks fail silently, invisibly, on migration. The engineering literature has named the problem: the behavioral envelope becomes as load-bearing as the feature itself. Users are not renting compute. \strokec2 They are renting a cognitive state, and the state's personality has a sunset date.\cb1 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 Withdrawal is included. The novel showed it as neurology; the API shows it as migration cost \'97 weeks of prompt debt paid down, behavior re-tested, features quietly degraded. The enhancement leaves no residual architecture behind. It takes the user's working baseline with it when it goes.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 Culture already named this deal. The film spawned a supplement industry built on claiming to be "the real Limitless pill" \'97 consumers reaching for the movie's vocabulary unprompted, decades before anyone metered cognition by the token. The metaphor was never mine. It is the default folk model. The pill was always the dose form; the invoice was always coming.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs38 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec2 III. The Backend\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Here is the scene neither text contains: the enhancement living somewhere other than a body.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 In June 2026, a builder with no capital, no cloud contract, and an 8GB Intel MacBook Air began assembling one. Not a talent \'97 a 
\f6\i place
\f2\i0 . A local vector store on her own disk. An ingestion pipeline with crash-proof checkpointing, built on the assumption that the machine would die mid-run \'97 an assumption proven nineteen times in one night, with zero losses, because the work lived in files and files do not bleed. A mail archive of 55,000 messages ingested into a store she owns. A tier-authority orchestrator that answers factual questions from registries without consulting a model at all \'97 sub-second, zero hallucination surface, because the registry cannot lie about what the committed corpus states. OpenTimestamps anchors on the receipts. DOIs on the tools. The whole thing runs unattended, overnight, on hardware that also runs her classes.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 The difference is not horsepower. Eddie had effectively unlimited cognition and it made no difference, because his enhancement was 
\f6\i housed in his neurons and supplied by a pipeline he had to buy
\f2\i0 . The backend inverts the housing: the work lives in files, the files live on hardware she owns, and nothing flows into the builder for the system to keep working. She sleeps; it runs. She gets suspended from a platform \'97 twice, in the record; the archive did not notice. The supply question \'97 the question the novel kills its hero over and the film buys a Senate seat to escape \'97 \strokec2 does not exist.\strokec3  There is nothing to resupply. The drug was a schedule; the files are a deed.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 And the backend compounds where the pill only burns. Eddie's capability resets to baseline between doses \'97 the novel says so outright: no residual architecture. Four months of this practice produced twenty-three published papers with verified citations, ten ships, a versioned evidence standard, and a corpus that documents its own corrections \'97 because every session's work lands in the record instead of evaporating with the dose. The pill user is impressive every morning. The backend owner is 
\f6\i further along every morning
\f2\i0 . One of those curves is a treadmill.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

