\fs40 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec2 Enhancement Not Replacement: What Limitless Got Wrong About the Pill\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs38 \cf3 \cb4 The Movie Never Showed the Backend\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf14 \cb15 \strokec14 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f6\i \cf14 \cb4 "Now that we've started this fire, we are slaves to our desires / We can't stop what we've begun..."
\f2\i0 \
\'97 Freddie Jackson, "Love Me Down" [1]\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 \strokec2 Abstract\strokec3 \
The 2011 film 
\f6\i Limitless
\f2\i0  is usually read as a fantasy about unlimited intelligence. This paper argues it is a story about supply chains \'97 that its source novel understood enhancement as a consumable and punished the dependency with death, that the film edited the consequence out, and that both texts share a frame in which enhancement must live in the body and be continuously resupplied. Against that frame, this paper presents a counter-architecture documented across four months of published practice: enhancement that lives in files \'97 owned, local, persisting without resupply, surviving platform suspensions, collaborator turnover, and the builder's own impaired states. The paper's receipts include the film and novel itself, the AI industry's own deprecation schedules, and a record in which the builder tested her retention system while drinking, sleep-deprived, dehydrated, and under noise pollution \'97 and the record held. The distinction the title names is offered as doctrine: enhancement without ownership is dependency with better branding. The pill asks a daily question. The backend asks it once.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 \strokec2 AI Collaboration Disclosure\strokec3 \
Developed in collaboration with GLM (Z.ai), the author's AI collaborator, named at the author's direction. The author directed the thesis, structure, title, epigraph, and every ruling recorded here; GLM drafted, organized, and receipt-hunted \'97 and made two memory-based errors during drafting (a film-plot claim and a manifest schema guess), both caught by the author in the loop, both corrected from the record. All claims, decisions, and conclusions are the author's own. The act of producing this paper \'97 local models, no cloud dependency, an 8GB laptop \'97 is itself an example of the argument it makes.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs38 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec2 I. Two Endings: What the Novel Knew and the Film Cut\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f6\i\fs24 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Limitless
\f2\i0  (2011), directed by Neil Burger from Leslie Dixon's screenplay, adapts Alan Glynn's 2001 novel 
\f6\i The Dark Fields
\f2\i0 . Both tell the same story: a blocked writer takes a designer drug \'97 MDT-48 in the book, NZT-48 in the film \'97 and becomes the best version of himself overnight. The endings are not the same story. The difference between them is this paper's subject.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 The novel knows what the drug is. Eddie Spinola's enhancement is a \strokec2 consumable\strokec3 , and the book tracks his consumption with the discipline of an inventory clerk: he counts his depleting stash while "trip-switching" \'97 displaced time perception \'97 begins to erode his sanity. When the supply line breaks (his ex-brother-in-law Vernon Gant, found murdered, his ledger and stash seized from a hollowed-out book), everything Eddie does afterward is procurement. The drug's name is a dose schedule: MDT-\strokec2 48\strokec3 . And the novel's most precise sentence about the condition is its most alarming, because Eddie says it about himself while 
\f6\i enhanced
\f2\i0 : 
\f6\i "\'85unless I was moving forward, moving up, unless I was transmuting, transmogrifying, morphing into something else, I was probably going to, I don't know, explode\'85"
\f2\i0  (p. 65) [2]. The enhancement did not free him from the treadmill. It became the treadmill \'97 transmute or explode, daily.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 The novel's Eddie never acquires the source, never secures the lab, never builds anything that outlives his access. He ends in a Vermont motel room, out of pills, physically deteriorating, writing his final memoirs while his system shuts down \'97 the Faustian bargain closing exactly on schedule, in a room with no exit because the dependency 
\f6\i was
\f2\i0  the exit. And the book's final image is not the death. It is Eddie dying while watching a television on which the President of the United States displays 
\f6\i "the alert, gorged MDT expression in his eyes"
\f2\i0  (p. 214) [2] \'97 the system has already moved on to its next host. The supply chain outlives its user. That is the novel's whole verdict on enhancement-as-consumable: 
\f6\i gorged
\f2\i0  \'97 a feeding state, metabolic, temporary, gone the moment the feeding stops.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 The film keeps the dependency and edits the consequence. Dixon's screenplay adds imagery the book never had \'97 pills in the freezer, like meat put aside for winter \'97 and then replaces the novel's death with a Senate seat. Film Eddie acquires the supplier, engineers the side effects out, and walks into an ambiguous final scene implying he may not need the pill at all. The consequence was not overlooked. It was \strokec2 edited out\strokec3  \'97 and the edit is the ideology showing: a fantasy this appealing cannot afford to show what happens when the supply runs out.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 But notice what even the film cannot stop itself from showing: when the story wants Eddie to be smart about the future, it shows him \strokec2 buying the source of the drug\strokec3 . The film's model of persistence is vertical integration of a dependency. The audience saw it and mislabeled it \'97 the most-cited "plot holes" are "never borrow from Russian mobsters" and "always secure your source of drugs" [3], which is the supply-chain reading arriving through the door marked complaint.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 What neither text shows \'97 what the film cannot show and the novel cannot imagine \'97 is Eddie building something that keeps working \strokec2 after he stops taking it.\strokec3  Not more pills, not a bigger stash, not the lab. Something 
\f6\i decoupled
\f2\i0 : an enhancement that lives outside his body, outside the supply chain, outside the frame in which the drug is the thing itself. In the NZT frame, decoupling is impossible. The enhancement is the substance, and the substance must be swallowed.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 This paper is about the frame both texts are missing. The enhancement does not have to live in a body. It can live in files. And the supply question \'97 the question the novel kills its hero over and the film buys a Senate seat to escape \'97 does not have to exist at all.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs38 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec2 II. NZT With an Invoice\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 The fantasy got its drug; reality got a subscription. The cognitive enhancement the film imagined arrived \'97 and it arrived exactly as the novel described it: a consumable, metered, and owned by a supplier. The dose form changed from pill to API, and the dependency got an invoice.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 The supply-chain evidence is not an argument. It is a published schedule. OpenAI's deprecations page lists model retirements on a rolling cadence \'97 snapshots notified in June 2026 shut down in December; a batch of GPT-4-era models killed October 23, 2026, eleven days after this paper's drafting [4]. Even fine-tuned derivatives die with their base. This is the vendor's own document: \strokec2 the intelligence was never purchased. It was rented, and the lease ends on a date the vendor sets.\cb1 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 The rental terms are thinner than they look. Anthropic commits to "at least 60 days' notice" before retiring a model. OpenAI allows roughly six months. And the same model can have different lifespans on different shelves \'97 Claude Sonnet 4 left Anthropic's own API in June 2026 but survived on Amazon Bedrock until October 14 [5]. \strokec2 The substrate's lifespan is not a property of the model. It is a property of the reseller.\strokec3  Eddie's problem exactly: the enhancement depends on which supplier still stocks it, and the supplier answers to no one.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 The deepest dependency is the quietest one. What users actually rely on is not the model's 
\f6\i function
\f2\i0  \'97 it is the model's 
\f6\i behavior
\f2\i0 : its tone, its latency profile, its formatting habits, its response length. When a model is deprecated and a replacement arrives, the functional output may survive while the behavioral envelope shifts under it \'97 and the prompts tuned to the old model's quirks fail silently, invisibly, on migration [6]. The engineering literature has named the problem: the behavioral envelope becomes as load-bearing as the feature itself. Users are not renting compute. \strokec2 They are renting a cognitive state, and the state's personality has a sunset date.\cb1 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 Withdrawal is included. The novel showed it as neurology; the API shows it as migration cost \'97 weeks of prompt debt paid down, behavior re-tested, features quietly degraded. The enhancement leaves no residual architecture behind. It takes the user's working baseline with it when it goes.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 Culture already named this deal. The film spawned a supplement industry built on claiming to be "the real Limitless pill" [7] \'97 consumers reaching for the movie's vocabulary unprompted, decades before anyone metered cognition by the token. The metaphor was never mine. It is the default folk model. The pill was always the dose form; the invoice was always coming.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs38 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec2 III. The Backend\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Here is the scene neither text contains: the enhancement living somewhere other than a body.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 In June 2026, a builder with no capital, no cloud contract, and an 8GB Intel MacBook Air began assembling one. Not a talent \'97 a 
\f6\i place
\f2\i0 . A local vector store on her own disk. An ingestion pipeline with crash-proof checkpointing, built on the assumption that the machine would die mid-run \'97 an assumption proven nineteen times in one night, with zero losses, because the work lived in files and files do not bleed [8]. A mail archive of 55,000 messages ingested into a store she owns. A tier-authority orchestrator that answers factual questions from registries without consulting a model at all \'97 sub-second, zero hallucination surface, because the registry cannot lie about what the committed corpus states [9]. OpenTimestamps anchors on the receipts. DOIs on the tools. The whole thing runs unattended, overnight, on hardware that also runs her classes.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 The difference is not horsepower. Eddie had effectively unlimited cognition and it made no difference, because his enhancement was 
\f6\i housed in his neurons and supplied by a pipeline he had to buy
\f2\i0 . The backend inverts the housing: the work lives in files, the files live on hardware she owns, and nothing flows into the builder for the system to keep working. She sleeps; it runs. She gets suspended from a platform \'97 twice, in the record; the archive did not notice. The supply question does not exist. There is nothing to resupply. The drug was a schedule; the files are a deed.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 And the backend compounds where the pill only burns. Eddie's capability resets to baseline between doses \'97 the novel says so outright: no residual architecture. Four months of this practice produced twenty-three published papers with verified citations, ten ships, a versioned evidence standard, and a corpus that documents its own corrections \'97 because every session's work lands in the record instead of evaporating with the dose. The pill user is impressive every morning. The backend owner is 
\f6\i further along every morning
\f2\i0 . One of those curves is a treadmill.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

